    {
      "id": "answer-care-for",
      "file": "answer-care-for.mp3",
      "text": "By treating their injuries, the nurse cared for injured people.",
      "kind": "model",
      "bytes": 56885,
      "sha256": "789e05a55af2c74567df2963d32451c6a6c9d88dd4ab8c7166e8c4c5bc0d0aea"
    },
    {
      "id": "answer-care-about",
      "file": "answer-care-about.mp3",
      "text": "Their concern showed that the neighbours cared about the affected families.",
      "kind": "model",
      "bytes": 65662,
      "sha256": "0f6d89322b0634e49dd72c313a8eab147f25c7b2b47bf7606a3c4aca8a13818f"
    },
    {
      "id": "page-09",
      "file": "page-09.mp3",
      "text": "Two days later, some homes still had no clean water. Outside their muddy houses, residents held empty containers and expressed their frustration. Elena agreed to speak for the neighbourhood. At the town hall, she presented their complaint to the mayor, together with photographs and a written request. Maya recorded the meeting. The mayor promised an update that afternoon. Maya wrote down the promise, but she knew she would need to check what happened next.",
      "kind": "section",
      "bytes": 427615,
      "sha256": "547194fd893e3799dc0bbcd9902152e86baa06799b558f06af1d5ae3ddacc08c"
    },
    {
      "id": "prediction-09",
      "file": "prediction-09.mp3",
      "text": "Is a promise the same as a completed action? What should Maya check next?",
